  "raw_text": "Step 1: First, we need to understand the behavior of the function \\( F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i} \\). We will calculate the first few terms of the sequence \\( z_n \\) to identify any patterns.\n\nStep 2: Calculate \\( z_1 = F(z_0) \\):\n\\[ z_1 = F\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i. \\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate \\( z_2 = F(z_1) \\):\n\\[ z_2 = F(1 + 274i) = \\frac{(1 + 274i) + i}{(1 + 274i) - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i}. \\]\nTo simplify this, multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i - 275 \\cdot 273}{1 + 273^2} = \\frac{1 + 2i - 74625}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{-74624 + 2i}{74530} = -\\frac{37312}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i. \\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate \\( z_3 = F(z_2) \\):\n\\[ z_3 = F\\left(-\\frac{37312}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) = \\frac{\\left(-\\frac{37312}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) + i}{\\left(-\\frac{37312}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) - i} = \\frac{-\\frac{37312}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{-\\frac{37312}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i}. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{-37312 + 37266i}{-37312 - 37264i} = \\frac{37312 - 37266i}{37312 + 37264i}. \\]\nMultiplying numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{(37312 - 37266i)(37312 - 37264i)}{(37312 + 37264i)(37312 - 37264i)} = \\frac{37312^2 - 37312 \\cdot 37266i - 37266 \\cdot 37312i + 37266 \\cdot 37264}{37312^2 + 37264^2} = \\frac{37312^2 - 2 \\cdot 37312 \\cdot 37266i + 37266 \\cdot 37264}{37312^2 + 37264^2} = \\frac{137}{137} = \\frac{1}{137} + i = z_0. \\]\n\nStep 5: From the above calculations, we observe that \\( z_3 = z_0 \\), indicating a periodicity of 3 in the sequence. Therefore, \\( z_{2002} = z_{2002 \\mod 3} = z_2 \\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-\\frac{37312}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i}<|im_end|>",
